// Type-check the HAND-WRITTEN declarations in src/types/.
//
// The main tsconfig sets `skipLibCheck: true`, which is meant to skip the
// declarations shipped in node_modules -- but it skips ALL .d.ts, including
// the ~3000 lines under src/types/ that describe the frozen JS core. Those are
// the most load-bearing types in the repo and were going unchecked: three of
// them turned out to misdescribe the core (ParkSpan.schedWait and
// TraceEvent.schedWait were `number` where the parser emits null;
// PollSpan.spawnLocId was `string | null` where the builder emits 0), each
// hidden behind a cast until the cast was removed.
//
// This config re-checks them with skipLibCheck OFF. It is a SEPARATE pass
// because turning the flag off in the main config would also check
// node_modules, which does not compile cleanly and is not ours to fix.
//
// probe.ts is included deliberately: it is the only thing exercising these
// declarations at real call shapes (generic preservation, overload selection,
// union narrowing). Note what neither it nor this config can do -- prove the
// declarations MATCH the JS. A confidently-wrong declaration still passes.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "skipLibCheck": false,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/types"]
}
